---
// src/pages/services/dishwasher-repair/kenmore-not-draining.astro
// Info Wave W2 — "kenmore dishwasher not draining" (1000 vol/mo KD 0). Brand sniper.
// Kenmore = badge only; the MAKER decides everything. Dishwasher prefix table in the lead:
// 665 = Whirlpool (HIGH), 587 = Whirlpool, 630 = Bosch (send to bosch-not-draining). Explicit
// note: dishwasher prefixes differ from laundry (665 laundry = different maker). Whirlpool-built
// Kenmore uses F9E1. Shared-platform honest line + mutual links. CA air-gap check. Safe DIY =
// filter/hose/high loop/disposal knockout/air gap; drain pump = tech. $89 residential.

import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ServiceHero from '../../../components/ServiceHero.astro';
import { MAIN_PHONE, toE164 } from '../../../data/branches';
import { BRANCH_LOCATIONS_GEO_NEUTRAL } from '../../../lib/build-location-array';

const phone = MAIN_PHONE;
const phoneRaw = MAIN_PHONE.replace(/\D/g, '');
const phoneHref = `tel:+1${phoneRaw}`;
const canonical = "https://samedayappliance.repair/services/dishwasher-repair/kenmore-not-draining/";

const title = "Kenmore Dishwasher Not Draining: Fix by Model — Same Day";
const description = "Kenmore dishwasher won't drain? Find your maker by model prefix: 665 = Whirlpool (F9E1), 630 = Bosch. Then the filter, hose, and air-gap fixes. $89.";

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "Why is my Kenmore dishwasher not draining?",
    a: "Kenmore is a store badge, not a manufacturer, so the first step is finding who actually built yours from the model-number prefix: 665 and 587 are Whirlpool-built (they use the F9E1 drain code), while 630 is Bosch-built. Once you know the maker, the standing water almost always traces to the same short list: a clogged lower filter, a kinked or clogged drain hose (or a low loop), a disposal knockout plug left in after a new disposal, a blocked sink air gap, or a failed drain pump. The first four are homeowner-checkable; the pump is the tech job. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair."
  },
  {
    q: "How do I tell who made my Kenmore dishwasher?",
    a: "Look at the model number on the door edge or tub rim — it starts with a three-digit prefix before a period. For dishwashers, 665.xxxxx and 587.xxxxx are Whirlpool-built, and 630.xxxxx is Bosch-built. Important: these dishwasher prefixes are not the same as Kenmore laundry prefixes, so don't use a washer/dryer maker chart here. Match the prefix, then follow the maker's fixes: Whirlpool-built units on this page, Bosch-built on our Bosch page."
  },
  {
    q: "What does F9E1 mean on a Kenmore dishwasher?",
    a: "F9E1 is the \"Long Drain\" code on Whirlpool-built Kenmore dishwashers (665 and 587 prefixes): the unit tried to pump out but didn't finish draining in time. It's a timeout, not a specific failed part. The documented causes are the drain path — clogged filter, kinked or clogged drain hose, blocked air gap, un-removed disposal knockout plug, or excess suds from dish soap. Older light-only Kenmore models blink the Clean light instead of showing a digital code. If your Kenmore is a 630 (Bosch-built), it uses Bosch's E24/E25 drain codes instead — see our Bosch page."
  },
  {
    q: "I have a Kenmore 630 dishwasher — is this the right page?",
    a: "A Kenmore 630 is Bosch-built, so the drain path, the filter design, and the error codes (E24 and E25, not F9E1) match Bosch rather than Whirlpool. You'll get the correct filter and pump-check steps on our Bosch dishwasher not draining page. If your Kenmore is a 665 or 587, you're in the right place — those are Whirlpool-built and everything on this page applies."
  },
  {
    q: "How do I clear a Kenmore dishwasher that won't drain?",
    a: "Safe, in order: scoop out the standing water, twist out and rinse the lower filter and clear the sump, check the drain hose behind the unit for a kink and confirm it loops up high before dropping to the drain, run the garbage disposal (a full one blocks the shared drain, and a new disposal may still have its knockout plug), and clear the sink air gap if you have one. Use only dishwasher detergent. Re-run a rinse cycle. If water still stands, it's the drain pump — that's our job."
  }
];

