  {schemaJsons.map((schema) => (<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />))}
</Fragment>

<ServiceHero
  section="services"
  slug="dishwasher-repair/kenmore-not-draining"
  eyebrow="Kenmore Dishwasher Not Draining · Find Your Maker · Same Day Southern California"
  title="Kenmore Dishwasher Not Draining: Fix by Model"
  subtitle="Kenmore is a badge — 665/587 is Whirlpool (F9E1), 630 is Bosch. Find your maker, then the filter, hose, disposal, and air-gap fixes. When to call."
  heroImageTitle="Kenmore Dishwasher Not Draining"
  showBranches={true}
/>

<!-- 01 ANSWER-FIRST -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">01 · Start with the model number</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Kenmore is a badge. Find who built yours first.</h2>

    <p><strong>Kenmore doesn't build dishwashers — the maker is hidden in the model-number prefix, and it decides your filter design and your error codes. For dishwashers: 665 and 587 are Whirlpool-built (they use the F9E1 drain code), and 630 is Bosch-built (E24/E25). Find the prefix on the door edge or tub rim, then follow that maker. Once you know it, standing water almost always traces to the same short list: a clogged filter, a kinked or clogged drain hose (or a low loop), a disposal knockout plug after a new disposal, a blocked sink air gap, or a failed drain pump. The first four are safe to check yourself. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair.</strong></p>

    <p>One trap worth calling out: <strong>Kenmore dishwasher prefixes are not the same as Kenmore laundry prefixes.</strong> A maker chart you found for a Kenmore washer or dryer won't map correctly to a dishwasher, so use the dishwasher table below.</p>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>Kenmore dishwasher maker by prefix</h3>
      <p><strong>665.xxxxx → Whirlpool-built.</strong> Uses F9E1. Everything on this page applies.<br/>
      <strong>587.xxxxx → Whirlpool-built.</strong> Same Whirlpool platform and fixes.<br/>
      <strong>630.xxxxx → Bosch-built.</strong> Uses E24/E25, not F9E1 — see our <a href="/services/dishwasher-repair/bosch-not-draining/">Bosch dishwasher not draining</a> page for the correct filter and pump-check steps.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 02 WHIRLPOOL-BUILT -->
<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">02 · If yours is 665 or 587 (Whirlpool)</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Same machine as a Whirlpool, KitchenAid, or Maytag.</h2>

    <p>A 665- or 587-series Kenmore is built on the <strong>same Whirlpool platform</strong> as KitchenAid and Maytag — same F9E1 drain code, same removable filter, same drain pump and check valve, same drain path to the sink. So the diagnosis is identical to those brands. F9E1 is a drain-timeout meaning the pump-out didn't finish in time; older light-only Kenmore models blink the Clean light instead of showing a code. The causes and the fixes are the drain-path list below. Same platform, brand pages: <a href="/services/dishwasher-repair/whirlpool-not-draining/">Whirlpool</a>, <a href="/services/dishwasher-repair/kitchenaid-not-draining/">KitchenAid</a>, <a href="/services/dishwasher-repair/maytag-not-draining/">Maytag</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 03 CAUSES -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">03 · The causes, in order</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Five causes, most common first.</h2>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>1. Clogged lower filter</h3>
      <p>The removable filter in the tub floor packs with food, glass grit, and grease. A partial clog slows the drain until F9E1 trips; a full one stops it. Twist it out, rinse, clear the sump.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>2. Drain hose — kink, clog, or low loop</h3>
      <p>Check behind the unit for a crushed or kinked hose, and confirm it loops up high before dropping to the drain. A low loop siphons sink water back and pools it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>3. Disposal knockout plug (new install)</h3>
      <p>A new garbage disposal ships with a solid plug sealing the dishwasher drain port. If it wasn't punched out, the dishwasher can't drain. The answer when a Kenmore stops draining right after disposal work.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>4. Blocked air gap (common in California)</h3>
      <p>Many California kitchens use an air gap — the chrome cap on the counter — to meet the plumbing code's backflow rule. It clogs and backs water into the dishwasher. Clearing it is a two-minute fix.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>5. Failed drain pump or check valve</h3>
      <p>When the whole path is clear and water still stands (or F9E1 returns), the drain pump has usually failed or its check valve is stuck. Needs a meter and a replacement part.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 04 SAFE CHECKS -->
<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">04 · What you can safely check</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Five safe steps before you call.</h2>

    <ol class="diag-list">
      <li><strong>Scoop the standing water</strong> with a cup and sponge so you can reach the filter.</li>
      <li><strong>Clean the filter.</strong> Twist out the lower filter, rinse it, and clear the sump — watch for broken glass.</li>
      <li><strong>Check the drain hose and high loop.</strong> Straighten any kink and route the hose so it loops up high before it drops.</li>
      <li><strong>Run the garbage disposal</strong> with water, and if it's a new disposal, confirm the knockout plug was removed.</li>
      <li><strong>Clear the air gap.</strong> Pop the chrome cap and clean it out. Use only dishwasher detergent, never dish soap.</li>
    </ol>

    <p class="callout"><strong>Where to stop:</strong> filter, hose, disposal, air gap, and a 30-second power-cycle are all safe. Don't remove the drain pump or open the control yourself, and mind the glass in the sump. If water still stands after these steps, it's the pump or the control — our job.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 05 WHEN TO CALL -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">05 · When to call us</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Clear path, still standing water? It's the pump.</h2>

    <p>Once the filter, hose, disposal, and air gap are verified clear and the tub still holds water (or F9E1 keeps returning), the drain pump or its check valve is the likely fault, and that needs testing and a replacement part. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair identify the maker from your model number first, then carry the right Whirlpool-platform or Bosch drain pump, so a confirmed failure is usually a one-visit fix. We check the upstream path first so we never swap a good pump that was fighting a clog, then quote before any work. <strong>$89 residential diagnostic, waived with the repair.</strong> Same-day across <a href="/los-angeles/dishwasher-repair/">Los Angeles</a>, Orange, and Ventura in most cases.</p>

    <p>Related: the general <a href="/services/dishwasher-repair/not-draining/">dishwasher not draining</a> page and the <a href="/services/dishwasher-repair/error-codes/">dishwasher error codes</a> guide. Whirlpool-built siblings: <a href="/services/dishwasher-repair/whirlpool-not-draining/">Whirlpool</a>, <a href="/services/dishwasher-repair/kitchenaid-not-draining/">KitchenAid</a>, <a href="/services/dishwasher-repair/maytag-not-draining/">Maytag</a>. Bosch-built 630: <a href="/services/dishwasher-repair/bosch-not-draining/">Bosch not draining</a>. Full coverage on the <a href="/services/dishwasher-repair/">dishwasher repair</a> hub. <a href="/book/">Book online</a> or call {phone}.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 06 FAQ -->
<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">06 · FAQ</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Kenmore dishwasher not draining: common questions.</h2>
    <div class="faq-list">
      {faqs.map(f => (<details class="faq-item"><summary>{f.q}</summary><p set:html={f.a}></p></details>))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 07 BOTTOM CTA -->
<section class="bottom-cta">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Kenmore dishwasher still full of water? Call today.</h2>
    <p>$89 diagnostic waived with repair. Same-day across LA, OC, Ventura. Phones answered 24/7.</p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a href={phoneHref} class="btn-primary">☎ Call {phone}</a>
      <a href="/book/" class="btn-secondary">Book Online</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</Layout>

